cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Indian Sign Language Recognition System
message: If you use this software or dataset, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Pramod
    given-names: Lakshmi Seema
  - family-names: Kumar
    given-names: Anjali S
abstract: >-
  Real-time recognition of Indian Sign Language fingerspelling (digits 0-9 and
  letters A-Z) from a webcam. Hand landmarks are extracted with MediaPipe Hands,
  normalised into a 42-dimensional feature vector, and classified by a small
  feed-forward neural network deployed as a quantised TFLite model. Includes a
  dataset of 117,139 labelled landmark vectors collected for the 36 classes.
keywords:
  - sign language recognition
  - indian sign language
  - hand gesture recognition
  - mediapipe
  - tensorflow
  - computer vision
license: Apache-2.0
date-released: 2024-05-01
